  "id": "kemadrin",
  "term": "Kemadrin",
  "definition": "Kemadrin is procyclidine hydrochloride, a drug with anticholinergic effects. It lowers acetylcholine activity in the striatum and may also increase dopamine activity, which can reduce akinesia, rigidity, and tremor linked to uncontrollable body movements.",
